On her account, Stause posted a tearful video. &#8220;G and I are no longer together,&#8221; she says in the clip. &#8220;We have agreed to treat this public separation with love and respect for each other. That&#8217;s not hard for me because I am in love with this person, and I don&#8217;t have all the information or the reasons.

&#8220;I feel like a little bit of a failure,&#8221; the All My Children alum also admitted. &#8220;I just have to heal and figure this out. It&#8217;s hard, it&#8217;s painful &#8212; I&#8217;m a lover girl, I swing big, I miss.&#8221;

That said, Stause was able to acknowledge that she&#8217;d had &#8220;an amazing four years with G,&#8221; and so &#8220;maybe it wasn&#8217;t a miss.&#8221; &#8220;I will always love G, and I don&#8217;t ever really see that changing,&#8221; she added. &#8220;This sucks, but everyone deserves to be happy, and I wish that for both of us.&#8221;

G Flip &#8212; whose song &#8220;Bed on Fire&#8221; recently debuted to No. 46 on the Hot Rock & Alternative Songs chart after it was featured in Off Campus &#8212; first started dating Stause in March 2022, the same year the former soap opera star appeared in the musician&#8217;s “Get Me Outta Here&#8221; music video. In May the following year, the pair got symbolically married in Las Vegas and made a tradition out of renewing their vows with each wedding anniversary.

